Z||000013||BAM-BAM||06-23-2000||07:33 PM||||  NO offense taken and as a matter of fact, is very easy to do. The hardest part was deciding how far forward to mount it. I was a little apprehensive about the drilling part, but in retrospect, I do some damn fine layout work, so why worry <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I was going to have custom gaskets made to take up the space on the inside edge of the mounting surface, but I'm concidering having it glassed on when I get around to TOM's scoop. I think it would look very clean as integral part of the rear decklid. If anyone decides in the future that they would like to give this spoiler application a try, just E-Mail me for details on layout and drilling. I will be more than happy to share my limited knowledge. Wow, does this make me at least, some kind of a pioneer in aftermarket Fiero applications?<P> Late, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||12
